  "finding": "Edition 157 reconstructs exactly the same evidence while reusing exact sampling coordinates and immutable reference calculations on fresh frame pixels. The exposed camera trace remains 34/42 correct observations, 8 withheld, 0 wrong overlaps and 0/30 hidden outputs, identical to 156. All three app comparisons reproduce exact reference evidence. 2/2 new generated cases meet their separate behavioral targets. Complete paired costs include the original verification. Defaults remain unchanged. On two alternating exposed-camera pairs, complete forced verification measured 147.26 seconds through published 156 and 135.86 seconds with precomputed terms (7.7% less time).",
  "validation": "57 selected Java checks and 164 desktop checks passed, with no failures or skipped cases. Two new generated app comparisons and one exposed-camera comparison passed visible-control, forced-replay, cold-restart and source-integrity checks. Complete reference/precomputed evidence matches exactly. Independent geometry and exact-evidence gates passed; harder behavioral targets and measured cost benefit are reported separately. These are scoped checks, not a rerun of every historical capability. Recorded tests only."
